  "hints": [
    "What should you track while scanning left to right?",
    "Keep the length of the current run; reset it to 0 on a zero day; remember the maximum seen.",
    "Update the best value after every day, not only when a streak ends, so a streak reaching the last day is counted."
  ],
  "editorial": "Scan once with `cur` (current run) and `best`. If `c_i > 0` then `cur += 1` else `cur = 0`; after each step `best = max(best, cur)`. Updating `best` inside the loop (not only on resets) is what handles a streak that runs to the final day. A common bug is forgetting that case, which the all-positive test catches.",
